# Wazuh Custom SSH Detection Rule

This file contains the custom rule used in the SOC lab to detect repeated SSH authentication failures associated with the same source IP.

## Rule configuration

```xml
<group name="local,sshd,authentication_failed,">
  <rule id="100100" level="10" frequency="5" timeframe="120">
    <if_matched_sid>5710</if_matched_sid>
    <same_srcip />
    <description>SSH: Repeated nonexistent-user login attempts from the same source IP within 120 seconds</description>
    <group>sshd,authentication_failed,invalid_login,</group>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1110.001</id>
    </mitre>
  </rule>
</group>
```

## Rule logic

- **Rule ID:** `100100`
- **Severity:** Level 10
- **Parent rule:** `5710`
- **Frequency:** Five matching events
- **Time window:** 120 seconds
- **Correlation:** Same source IP
- **MITRE ATT&CK:** `T1110.001` — Password Guessing

## Validation

The rule triggered during controlled testing in Wazuh log testing and a corresponding alert was observed in the dashboard.

## Deployment note

This is a portable documentation example, not a replacement for the complete system `local_rules.xml` file. When deploying it, place the rule inside the appropriate existing Wazuh group structure, check for duplicate rule IDs, validate it with `wazuh-logtest`, and restart the manager only after the configuration is confirmed valid.
